@Gerald Butler No Friend, you’re not screwed at all : you’re « just » overwhelmed. I get it, trust me, I do. So was I too for the past three years… But maybe you’d like to talk to me and tell me how you’re feeling today ? I’m always listening kind stranger.
Sincerely yours,
Tchiñdā

@ccharles848  I could have written your comment verbatim. I believe I understand. 
The most important realization I’ve made is that when I have suicidal thoughts, I’m experiencing inner turmoil and/or feeling trapped in a situation I really don’t like. Suicidal thoughts are, in a way,  my salvation because I realize I’m never really trapped — there’s still an  avenue of escape. That buys me time to come up with a way or ways to reduce my pain. Sometimes I go get therapy and sometimes I come up with changes I need to make. Seems like I have to hit a certain level of pain before I get motivated to make changes in my life. And to be 100% honest, I’m too big a chicken to go through with suicide. What if I tried, didn’t succeed, and wound up in a vegetative state? No thanks!  
If none of what I’ve written rings true for you, then sister - or mister - know that you are not alone. I’m glad you commented; it’s a good thing to open up. I’ll be thinking of you and praying for you. We’re kind of on the same team.

